  "Question": "After combining like terms, the polynomial \\(2x^2+mx-5x+3\\) has no first-degree term in \\(x\\). Find the value of \\(m\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The first-degree terms combine to give \\((m-5)x\\). Having no first-degree term means that its coefficient satisfies \\(m-5=0\\), so \\(m=5\\).",
